# Retire policy 2026-11-20: still in production in 2026 with no announced end; retire dates commented out. Revisit when an end is announced.
# Vauxhall Mokka B compact SUV, 2021 onwards.
#
# The Mokka B: the smaller, lower car on the CMP platform with the
# Vauxhall Vizor face, sold from 12 April 2021 and still current in
# facelifted form. The Mokka Electric shares the body and is not separately
# represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opel_Mokka
#
# Dimensions 4.151 x 1.791 x 1.531 m, wheelbase 2.557 m (Wikipedia infobox).
# The car is 129 mm shorter, 16 mm wider and 115 mm lower than the Mokka A.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true level side elevation; the flank is
# traced from it.
#
# Colours: grade (a), the All-new Mokka price and specification guide of
# 22 September 2020 for model year 2021: White Jade brilliant; Diamond
# Black, Quartz Grey and Voltaic Blue metallic; Mamba Green and Power Red
# premium metallic. Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39, provisional.
# Speed 200 km/h. Comfort 80/450, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 80. Class 1.
# Dates: intro April 2021; retire dates commented out (still in production in 2026).
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-mokka-b.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vauxhall-mokka-b.dae. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-mokka-b/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: the shared launch-era Mokka/Mokka-e shell is modelled
# with a black roof, and no electric-only badging is added. The wheel spokes,
# lamp internals, lettering and bumper inserts are simplified.


obj=citycar
name=VauxhallMokkaB(WhiteJade)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=12
intro_year=2021
intro_month=4
#retire_year=2043
#retire_month=6
speed=200
length=3
class=1
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=80
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=450

